# Canonical Redis ACL entry for the inventory-v2 application user.
#
# Copy the `user` line below into `acl/users.acl` on the central Redis
# platform, replace <PASSWORD> with the real secret, replace <PREFIX> with the
# value of REDIS_KEY_PREFIX (WITHOUT the trailing colon — default
# "inventory-v2"), then run:
#
#   redis-cli -a "$REDIS_ADMIN_PASSWORD" ACL LOAD
#   redis-cli -a "$REDIS_ADMIN_PASSWORD" ACL GETUSER inventory-v2
#
# Both ACL axes are required and are INDEPENDENT of each other:
#   ~<PREFIX>:*  -> keys (cache, locks, BullMQ, rate limits)
#   &<PREFIX>:*  -> Pub/Sub channels (BullMQ events, Socket.IO shared adapter)
#
# Redis 7 creates users with `resetchannels` by default, so a user that only
# has `~<PREFIX>:*` will get `NOPERM No permissions to access a channel` on
# `psubscribe <PREFIX>:#/#*`. That exact pattern is emitted by
# @socket.io/redis-adapter because RedisIoAdapter sets the adapter `key` option
# to `${REDIS_KEY_PREFIX}:` (ioredis keyPrefix does not apply to Pub/Sub).
# Required channels (root namespace):
#   PSUBSCRIBE <PREFIX>:#/#*
#   SUBSCRIBE  <PREFIX>:-request#/#, <PREFIX>:-response#/#,
#              <PREFIX>:-response#/#<uid>#
#   PUBLISH    <PREFIX>:#/#… (and BullMQ channels under the same prefix)
#
# A broad `+@all -@admin -@dangerous` command policy is used here on purpose:
# ioredis' ready check needs INFO, ioredis 5 sends CLIENT SETINFO, and BullMQ
# needs EVAL/EVALSHA Lua scripting in addition to stream/list/sorted-set/hash
# commands. If your platform enforces a stricter allowlist, keep at least
# @pubsub, @scripting, @blocking, @stream, @list, @sortedset, @hash, @set,
# @string, @keyspace, @read, @write, @slow and @connection. Key and channel
# patterns remain the actual isolation boundary; never use `&*` or `~*` in a
# shared Redis.
user inventory-v2 on ><PASSWORD> ~<PREFIX>:* &<PREFIX>:* +@all -@admin -@dangerous
